{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Addition Property of Inequality.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Addition Property of Inequality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"addition property of inequality addition property of inequality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Addition Property of Inequality.md","fileName":"Addition Property of Inequality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Addition Property of Inequality","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Linear Inequalities and Intervals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Inequalities and Intervals","Number Line","Linear Inequality in One Variable","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Addition Property of Inequality.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Addition Property of Inequality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"addition property of inequality addition property of inequality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Addition Property of Inequality.md","fileName":"Addition Property of Inequality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Addition Property of Inequality","heading":"Addition Property of Inequality","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The addition property of inequality states that adding the same real number to both sides preserves their order. If (a<b), then\n\n$$a+c<b+c.$$\n\nSubtracting the same number also preserves order because it adds an opposite. Geometrically, both values shift by the same distance on the [[Number Line]], so neither passes the other. This property allows constant terms to be removed while solving a [[Linear Inequality in One Variable]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Inequalities and Intervals","Number Line","Linear Inequality in One Variable","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"e